WEBVTT

00:00:11.004 --> 00:00:14.244
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> <b>How to survive coming to study in the UK</b>

00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:22.849
You have a place to study in the UK, you have your visa, and you’ve found accommodation,

00:00:23.018 --> 00:00:24.305
and you’re ready to go.

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:29.542
You’re very excited – but you also have so many questions!

00:00:31.215 --> 00:00:32.078
But don’t worry.

00:00:32.495 --> 00:00:36.523
This guide, compiled with the help of many international students,

00:00:37.093 --> 00:00:39.932
aims to help make your first year at university

00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:43.549
or college everything that you have always hoped for.

00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:46.831
Here are four important tips:

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:54.821
<b>1 Pack intelligently before you come.</b>

00:00:55.590 --> 00:01:00.979
It’s never too early to start packing! Make sure you bring these things:

00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:03.579
Suitable clothes.

00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:07.473
The UK may be colder and wetter than your country,

00:01:07.795 --> 00:01:10.814
so bring warm clothes and a raincoat!

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:14.750
Adaptors.

00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:17.904
 You can of course buy these in the UK,

00:01:18.222 --> 00:01:22.143
but you will probably want to use your laptop and phone immediately.

00:01:25.191 --> 00:01:26.396
Kitchen equipment.

00:01:27.269 --> 00:01:29.801
If you’re planning to cook some of your meals,

00:01:30.094 --> 00:01:35.305
pack some essential cooking equipment so you can start cooking from day one.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:51.984
<b>2 Get to know your city.</b>

00:01:53.175 --> 00:01:56.914
Before you come, have a good look online at the area

00:01:56.915 --> 00:02:01.144
where you’re going to live, for example, on Google Street View.

00:02:01.595 --> 00:02:05.625
Then check all the places you would like to visit in your new city.

00:02:06.419 --> 00:02:12.245
There are lots of ways of making city travel cheaper, like the Oyster card in London.

00:02:13.837 --> 00:02:21.796
You can also get a discount at many places like museums or cinemas with your student ID card.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.867
<b>3 Learn to manage your money.</b>

00:02:40.295 --> 00:02:44.725
You may find you have a lot of money in your bank account at the beginning of term,

00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:48.006
but after a few weeks, it’s all gone!

00:02:50.293 --> 00:02:53.510
Try to make a spending plan and stick to it.

00:02:55.516 --> 00:03:02.828
Many students get part-time jobs, for example, in a bar or café, or sometimes on campus.

00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:08.541
Jobs are also good to put on your CV,

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:11.156
and are good work experience, too.

00:03:25.848 --> 00:03:28.040
<b>4 Make friends.</b>

00:03:29.048 --> 00:03:32.585
It can be a bit frightening to come to a new country on your own.

00:03:33.185 --> 00:03:36.641
But don’t worry, there are many ways to make friends.

00:03:37.857 --> 00:03:43.214
All universities have lots of clubs for all kinds of free-time activities

00:03:43.547 --> 00:03:48.537
like sports, games, music, and other more unusual things.

00:03:51.932 --> 00:03:54.730
You can find out about them in the first week of term,

00:03:55.042 --> 00:03:57.234
usually called Fresher’s Week.

00:03:59.442 --> 00:04:05.820
If you’re a bit homesick, almost all cultures have their own societies which organize events,

00:04:06.352 --> 00:04:09.351
so you can meet other students from your country.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:29.640
So those are four tips for how to survive coming to study in the UK.

00:04:30.017 --> 00:04:32.292
Good luck, and have a great time!